@startuml dagents_project_context
title Dagents project context: one source agent per source, one GMA for multi-source computation

left to right direction
skinparam backgroundColor #F7F3EA
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Aptos"
skinparam roundCorner 12
skinparam ArrowColor #53635B
skinparam ArrowThickness 2

skinparam rectangle {
  BackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  BorderColor #B9C2BB
  FontColor #15201B
}
skinparam database {
  BackgroundColor #EEF3EF
  BorderColor #7E9287
}
skinparam actor {
  BorderColor #2E6F4E
  FontColor #15201B
}

actor "Business user\nor app owner" as Owner
actor "Platform operator" as Operator

rectangle "Consumer backend\nWatchdog / Datalytics /\nNL2SQL demo" as Product #FFFFFF
rectangle "Dagents framework services\ncatalog, pipelines, model jobs,\nworkload generation" as Services #F0E2C8

package "Data sources" as Sources {
  database "Source 1\nDatabase" as Source1
  database "Source 2\nEvent stream" as Source2
  database "Source 3\nObject files" as Source3
}

package "One local agent per source" as CMAs {
  rectangle "CMA / LMA 1\nlocal computation agent" as CMA1 #DCEBE1
  rectangle "CMA / LMA 2\nlocal computation agent" as CMA2 #DCEBE1
  rectangle "CMA / LMA 3\nlocal computation agent" as CMA3 #DCEBE1
}

rectangle "GMA\nglobal / multi-source\ncomputation agent" as GMA #DCE7F1

cloud "Kubernetes or app runtime\nwhere workloads run" as Runtime #EDE8DD

Owner --> Product : asks for answers,\nmodels, or automation
Operator --> Services : deploys and observes\nframework workloads

Product --> Services : uses framework APIs
Product --> GMA : requests multi-source view

Source1 --> CMA1 : local data
Source2 --> CMA2 : local data
Source3 --> CMA3 : local data

CMA1 --> GMA : source profile,\nmodel output
CMA2 --> GMA : source profile,\nmodel output
CMA3 --> GMA : source profile,\nmodel output

Services --> CMA1 : deploys and triggers\nlocal work
Services --> GMA : registers agents,\nplans aggregate work
Services --> Runtime : generates manifests\nand workload plans
GMA --> Product : combined result,\nsummary, action

note bottom of CMA2
  The codebase names this local agent LMA.
  The presentation can describe it as a
  per-source computation agent (CMA).
end note
@enduml
